From: fozzfut <vanolia13@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:24:50 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] PartDesign: Chamfer and Fillet report an invalid result
 instead of Up-to-date

OCCT can return an invalid solid from a chamfer without an error, for
example when the Size on a face is larger than the radius of the rim
there (the contact curve folds). The feature used to accept it and turn
Up-to-date. Now the result is checked after makeElementShape (BRepCheck
on the faces that are not faces of the base, plus shell closure and
orientation):
- a new (Consistent) chamfer fails with "Chamfer gives an invalid solid
  with Size on FaceN; try Flip direction" (Equal distance: "try a
  smaller Size");
- a Legacy chamfer keeps its result and prints one console warning, so
  old documents do not break;
- a fillet prints one console warning.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
